dg$, NULL, $dg$CONTROLLER_AND_PROCESSOR$dg$, $dg$RECOMMENDED_BY_DATAGUARD$dg$, $dg$STRONG$dg$, $dg$QUARTERLY$dg$, $dg$SECURITY$dg$, $dg$HIGH$dg$, $dg$DataGuard default risk classification: High. Unauthorised processing is expressly named in section 27(1) and is where security failures and purpose limitation failures overlap.$dg$, $dg$Identify the systems holding personal data, select proportionate safeguards against unauthorised processing, assign an owner, and produce operating evidence.$dg$, $dg$Control and review automated processing and extracts of personal data$dg$, $dg$HIGH$dg$, $dg$ACTIVE$dg$, $dg$1.0.0$dg$, $dg$ACT_EXPLICIT$dg$, $dg$NONE$dg$, $dg$Section 27(1) lists negligent loss and unauthorised destruction, alteration, access and processing as separate harms. DataGuard maps each to its own control so that partial coverage is visible.$dg$, ARRAY[$dg$Implemented$dg$, $dg$Partially implemented$dg$, $dg$Not implemented$dg$, $dg$Not applicable$dg$, $dg$I do not know$dg$]::text[], ARRAY[$dg$Access Control Procedure$dg$, $dg$Data Flow Diagram$dg$, $dg$Test Data Management Policy$dg$, $dg$Integration Register$dg$]::text[], true, 37) on conflict (framework_code, version_code, control_id) do update set subsection=excluded.subsection, paragraph=excluded.paragraph, legal_reference=excluded.legal_reference, legal_requirement=excluded.legal_requirement, control_title=excluded.control_title, control_description=excluded.control_description, plain_language_question=excluded.plain_language_question, why_this_matters=excluded.why_this_matters, implementation_guidance=excluded.implementation_guidance, expected_state=excluded.expected_state, response_type=excluded.response_type, applicability=excluded.applicability, applicability_question=excluded.applicability_question, role_scope=excluded.role_scope, evidence_required=excluded.evidence_required, evidence_strength=excluded.evidence_strength, evidence_review_frequency=excluded.evidence_review_frequency, risk_category=exclude